        {
          "kicker": "Discipline meltdown",
          "heading": "Fiji Latui collect four yellows and a red in Ireland XV rout",
          "body": "Fiji's Latui side were reduced to 12 men for a spell on Friday as an Ireland XV ran in nine tries at Virgin Media Park in Cork. Tighthead Mesake Doge was binned for a high tackle on Ireland's Todd Lawlor. Within 30 seconds of his return he was shown a second yellow and a 20-minute red for collapsing a scrum. Isaia Lotawa's no-arms tackle cost a penalty try, and Apisalome Kuruisaqila was carded for a deliberate knock-on. Pita Lesivoukionoilau's interception and Jope Naseara's breakaway were Fiji's two tries."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
