          "kicker": "Captain's code",
          "heading": "Maro Itoje rejects win-at-all-costs mentality before England face the All Blacks",
          "body": "England captain Maro Itoje says his Christian faith sets limits on what he would do to win, and he named performance-enhancing drugs and betting on the game as examples. “Integrity is really important,” he said, in a week dominated by Springboks head coach Rassie Erasmus's six-match ban for questioning whether officials were match-fixing. Itoje also called for referees to be respected. He wants Saturday's test against New Zealand at Twickenham to deliver back-to-back wins over the All Blacks for the first time since 2003."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji collect five cards in Ireland XV rout",
