    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-21",
      "edition": "Saturday 21 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Ireland XV",
          "heading": "Ireland XV run in nine tries as Fijian Latui collect five cards",
          "body": "The Ireland XV learned little from Friday's rout at Virgin Media Park, where the visitors were shown five cards in the first half and played with 12 men for a spell. Captain Gus McCarthy and Connacht's Daniel Ryan scored two tries each. Out-half Joey Carbery set up Ryan's opener and later dived under the posts after Fijian tighthead Mesake Doge was sent off for a second yellow. Paul Boyle withdrew late from the Ireland XV bench with a neck issue, and Scott Penny took his place."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
