      "edition": "Saturday 21 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Lineout call",
          "heading": "Quesada hands Ortombina Italy's lineout calls and Miotti a debut against Fiji",
          "body": "Italy head coach Gonzalo Quesada has made only two changes from the 14-19 defeat by Argentina in Genoa for Saturday's Nations Championship test v Fiji in Udine. Alessandro Ortombina starts at lock, with Federico Ruzza dropping to the bench. Quesada said Ortombina is at the right level to lead the lineout and brings physicality that can help against Fiji. Montpellier fly-half Domingo Miotti makes his Italy debut in place of Paolo Garbisi. The Italian federation's analysis notes Fiji had lineout-throwing problems in their 43-15 defeat by Ireland in Dublin."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
