          "kicker": "U20 win",
          "heading": "Scotland U20 edge Ireland 31-29 in Cork as Irish leveller drifts wide",
          "body": "Scotland U20 spoiled Ireland's U20s opener at Musgrave Park on Friday. They conceded five tries to a home pack dominant at scrum and maul but won through more accurate goal-kicking. Ireland out-half Paul Neary's late conversion to tie the game drifted wide. Scotland centre Harry Soboil was sin-binned for repeated infringements in an error-strewn first half, but wing Rory Caldwell and locks James Dalrymple and Christian Lindsay all crossed as the visitors punished two Irish yellow cards."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
