          "heading": "Felipe Contepomi accuses Montpellier of broken deal as Piccardo misses France test",
          "body": "Argentina head coach Felipe Contepomi says centre Justo Piccardo's absence from Saturday's test against France was forced rather than chosen. Speaking on Friday, he said Piccardo had played 11 straight weeks and showed a GPS drop-off against Italy that pointed to fatigue. He accused Montpellier director of rugby Bernard Laporte and manager Joan Caudullo of breaking their agreement. Laporte told Rugbyrama that the June deal held only if the club avoided injuries, and cited a back-line crisis including Dimitri Delibes and Auguste Cadot."
