          "heading": "Every Wallabies match at home World Cup to screen free on Nine",
          "body": "Nine Entertainment will broadcast half of the 52 matches at next year's men's World Cup in Australia, including all of the Wallabies' games, free on its channels and the 9Now streaming service, Rugby World reports. The remaining games go to subscription service Stan Sport, which also carries captain Harry Wilson's side against Wales in Cardiff. In Britain, ITV's deal with World Rugby, announced in July, keeps all 52 games free-to-air for a 24-team tournament running from 1 October to 13 November 2027."
